y":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T04:53:53-07:00","id":1301863,"title":"","content":"Also I recall Vance posting a link to an errata google drive--does anyone have that handy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T05:39:02-07:00","id":1301868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301861#post1301861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While this is true, it seems like 15 auto successes on an attack roll (and therefore as dice to the damage die) for a size 1 battle group is, uh, a tad much? Especailly as the battle group attacks an entire range band. Like, if your SOLAR SWORD PRINCESS, Melee 5 Dex 5, max excellency (parry 12, burn a wp for 13), your auto hit with some to spare. 15m, 1wp, and -2i a turn seem relatively cheap if a lunar elder can end a fight with 5-10 opponents in 2 turns<br /> (And if your a lunar elder bringing a Size 3-4 battle group, that's gonna be in the low twenties in auto successes).</div> </div> </div> </div>a)Yes, but that's a very good roll from the Lunar, even if they spent 10m on the roll. So 25 motes have been spent, and they rolled very well.<br /> <br /> b) It's Essence 4. In 2 turns, a single Essence 4 Dawn has probably killed about 3000 soldiers. Or just killed this Lunar who's been standing around ordering soldiers.<br /> <br /> c)Essence 4 Dawns have their own defensive tricks. Dodge, Resistance, etc. Our Essence 5 Dawn once got hit by an attack that did 53 dice of damage. It put him... on -1s.<br /> If you're pointing out the incredible offensive power of an Essence 4 Lunar general, then presumably you're comparing her to other Essence 4 builds, like stamina/strength berzerker, DBT/martial artist, Invincible Sword Princess, Solar Martial Artist, Solar stealth assassin, 5 Immaculate Monks, etc.<br /> <br /> My experience is a lot of builds that look amazing in white room actually come up against a whole heap of enemy tricks people didn't consider.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say it doesn't seem very powerful to me, because it does. But it's at the top of a tree that actually mostly isn't about mass combat. Also, your battle group is going to get carved to pieces quickly, because it's benefits are all offensive, not defensive. You're going to need to combine it with some charms from other trees to rally for numbers, because battle groups get carved up pretty quickly by PCs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T05:39:37-07:00","id":1301869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301862#post1301862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hm...that's true. I still don't like &quot;no ninja can sneak up on me&quot; as an essence 1 charm though?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty fair.<br /> <br /> Or... well, to be honest, I don't think it's terrible for the game. Ninja-stealth is very problematic game and balance wise. But it is something the game is designed to allow you to build for, and the charm shuts it down pretty harshly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T05:47:04-07:00","id":1301871,"title":"","content":"Regarding Secret Sense, it's going to be rewritten to allow Ambush if failed a la word of Vance on discord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T05:49:44-07:00","id":1301874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301862#post1301862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hm...that's true. I still don't like &amp;quot;no ninja can sneak up on me&amp;quot; as an essence 1 charm though?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not though. It's a charm that forces assassins to have good guile to block the read intentions roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T05:52:56-07:00","id":1301875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301869#post1301869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's pretty fair.<br /> <br /> Or... well, to be honest, I don't think it's terrible for the game. Ninja-stealth is very problematic game and balance wise. But it is something the game is designed to allow you to build for, and the charm shuts it down pretty harshly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure it's all that harsh, no ambush sucks for the ambusher, sure, but they're still in hidden, still get to make unexpected attacks, the Lunar doesn't know where they are, or who they are, just that someone or something is there, a lot of the advantages of being sneaky-sneaky are still present. I actually like it for creating something of a stealth halfway house as pretty much every other charm interaction with stealth tends towards a binary or you're either perfectly hidden or you're totally revealed.<br /> It sure does feel powerful, but I'm just not sure it really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/membe