ces assassins to have good guile to block the read intentions roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As written, if you fail on the Read Intentions Roll it's down graded to a suprise attack, which is much much better than an ambush. An ambush reduces the defense to 0, a suprise reduces it by 2--this is getting errat'd apparently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T06:03:34-07:00","id":1301879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301868#post1301868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> a)Yes, but that's a very good roll from the Lunar, even if they spent 10m on the roll. So 25 motes have been spent, and they rolled very well.<br /> <br /> b) It's Essence 4. In 2 turns, a single Essence 4 Dawn has probably killed about 3000 soldiers. Or just killed this Lunar who's been standing around ordering soldiers.<br /> <br /> c)Essence 4 Dawns have their own defensive tricks. Dodge, Resistance, etc. Our Essence 5 Dawn once got hit by an attack that did 53 dice of damage. It put him... on -1s.<br /> If you're pointing out the incredible offensive power of an Essence 4 Lunar general, then presumably you're comparing her to other Essence 4 builds, like stamina/strength berzerker, DBT/martial artist, Invincible Sword Princess, Solar Martial Artist, Solar stealth assassin, 5 Immaculate Monks, etc.<br /> <br /> My experience is a lot of builds that look amazing in white room actually come up against a whole heap of enemy tricks people didn't consider.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say it doesn't seem very powerful to me, because it does. But it's at the top of a tree that actually mostly isn't about mass combat. Also, your battle group is going to get carved to pieces quickly, because it's benefits are all offensive, not defensive. You're going to need to combine it with some charms from other trees to rally for numbers, because battle groups get carved up pretty quickly by PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hadn't noticed the defensive issue.<br /> b is iffy, if only because I feel like that many auto successes is pushing the math regardless of where it is in the game<br /> A and C are fair--I misread at first, and thought it was dice not dice added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T06:23:26-07:00","id":1301882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301877#post1301877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah thanks. I'm not on the discord--it got too busy for me to track everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. I'm just wondering if you would get another Per + Awareness roll to spot the assailant after Secret Sense fails to penetrate Guile. Worth asking in ask the devs, methinks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T06:48:04-07:00","id":1301889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301861#post1301861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While this is true, it seems like 15 auto successes on an attack roll (and therefore as dice to the damage die) for a size 1 battle group is, uh, a tad much? Especailly as the battle group attacks an entire range band. Like, if your SOLAR SWORD PRINCESS, Melee 5 Dex 5, max excellency (parry 12, burn a wp for 13), your auto hit with some to spare. 15m, 1wp, and -2i a turn seem relatively cheap if a lunar elder can end a fight with 5-10 opponents in 2 turns<br /> (And if your a lunar elder bringing a Size 3-4 battle group, that's gonna be in the low twenties in auto successes).</div> </div> </div> </div>Curious how that plays out in practice.<br /> -On the one hand my experience tells me that not getting crashed while facing 5-10 opponents is extremely impressive.<br /> -On the other I agree that large battle group numbers like this can be to put it politely... alarming in that they have the potential to crash everyone in late round one then follow up with an attack capable of killing multiple people before anyone gets chance to go in round 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T06:49:37-07:00","id":1301890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301868#post1301868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">c)Essence 4 Dawns have their own defensive tricks. Dodge, Resistance, etc. Our Essence 5 Dawn once got hit by an attack that did 53 dice of damage. It put him... on -1s.<br /> If you're pointing out the incredible offensive power of an Essence 4 Lunar general, then presumably you're comparing her to other Essence 4 builds, like stamina/strength berzerker, DBT/martial artist, Invincible Sword Princess, Solar Martial Artist, Solar stealth assassin, 5 Immaculate Monks, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't this 53 dice correspond to removing successes using 1,s and 2s? I don't know how 53 dice of damage would only do very little damage even with resistance unless he had a bunch of tricks which reduced successes based on what they rolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T06:49:37-07:00","id":1301891,"title":"","content":"double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T06:52:29-07:00","id":1301892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301890#post1301890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't this 53 dice correspond to removing successes using 1,s and 2s? I don't know how 53 dice of damage would only do very little damage even with resistance unless he had a bunch of tricks which reduced successes based on what they rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The 'solution' if your a Melee dawn seeing this coming is the perfect block (Heavenly Guardian right? I'm AFB) and rush now that I think about it with my full facilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T07:18:38-07:00","id":1301895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301890#post1301890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't this 53 dice correspond to removing successes using 1,s and 2s? I don't know how 53 dice of damage would only do very little damage even with resistance unless he had a bunch of tricks which reduced successes based on what they rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adamant Skin, Ruin-Abasing Shrug, and... I've forgotten it, that low-level Resistance charm that gives you a ton of extra -0 health levels.<br /> <br /> My point is, the enemies an Essence 4 Lunar warlord will face have their own set of powerful charms that you have to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T07:20:01-07:00","id":1301896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301879#post1301879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I hadn't noticed the defensive issue.<br /> b is iffy, if only because I feel like that many auto successes is pushing the math regardless of where it is in the game<br /> A and C are fair--I misread at first, and thought it was dice not dice added.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I thought there was a Lunar charm that let you make a reflexive command roll to boost their Defence and Soak, but I can't find it anywhere. Maybe I just imagined it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T07:21:58-07:00","id":1301898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301895#post1301895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Adamant Skin, Ruin-Abasing Shrug, and... I've forgotten it, that low-level Resistance charm that gives you a ton of extra -0 health levels.<br /> <br /> My point is, the enemies an Essence 4 Lunar warlord will face have their own set of powerful charms that you have to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure but doing an automatic 20+ successes that ignores rolling altogether would eventually cause problems for him. Ruin-Abasing shrug would flat out no longer work int his case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T07:47:38-07:00","id":1301905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301889#post1301889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-On the other I agree that large battle group numbers like this can be to put it politely... alarming in that they have the potential to crash everyone in late round one then follow up with an attack capable of killing multiple people before anyone gets chance to go in round 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't that kind of create an incentive to fight armies with armies?<br /> <br /> I swear, battle groups might be the thing I get the most mixed messages from with regards to other people's accounts of how they're perceived or been seen to play out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T07:56:18-07:00","id":1301908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301898#post1301898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure but doing an automatic 20+ successes that ignores rolling altogether would eventually cause problems for him. Ruin-Abasing shrug would flat out no longer work int his case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Command rolls boost attack, not damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T08:02:53-07:00","id":1301910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301905#post1301905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't that kind of create an incentive to fight armies with armies?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that you could use this charm to boost your unit of 10 bodyguards, which is hardly an army... but 10 bodyguards isn't even going to last an entire round against a circle of Exalts, so this is probably at its nastiest when buffing<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I swear, battle groups might be the thing I get the most mixed messages from with regards to other people's accounts of how they're perceived or been seen to play out. </div> </div> </div>They're certainly something where, when people are talking about them on this forum, some people's experience is very different from mine.<br /> <br /> Though I'll also say that my own experience of them is probably quite swingy. Sometimes they've been quite scary, other times they go down really fast. Most of the time they mostly make a nice tar pit to stop PCs killing the NPC heroes too quickly.<br /> I think there's a lot of variables with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:02:49-07:00","id":1301985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301910#post1301910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I'll also say that my own experience of them is probably quite swingy. Sometimes they've been quite scary, other times they go down really fast. Most of the time they mostly make a nice tar pit to stop PCs killing the NPC heroes too quickly.<br /> I think there's a lot of variables with them.</div> </div> </div> </div> That aligns with my own experiences. Of particular note, I'm in is Sidereals game and due to that splat's relationship with armour its pretty easy for a single area attack to put most of the circle into negative initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:37:42-07:00","id":1301999,"title":"","content":"I still think Invincible Beast Warrior Empowerment is overtuned.<br /> With size + might autosuccesses, a lunar is looking at potentially +8 successes on every roll of his battle group before orders. An average command roll with no excellency will net another 5, bringing it to 13, which is enough for the bg to auto hit any solar not using a perfect (or cap breaking with Dodge which is not sustainable).<br /> <br /> Yes the tankiest solar will take this, but basically nothing else in the game can put up a meaningful defence. And the bg can do this every turn, because we're just looking at 1 scenelong for investment.<br /> <br /> (BGs with orders already throw the numeric balance of the system out of wack, this is looking at effectively doubling the dice we pile on top of a BG action)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8977-sigfriedmcwild","name":"sigfriedmcwild","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8977_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T14:03:28-07:00","id":1302006,"title":"","content":"Skimmed last page and didn't see this linked-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SNao6N1Etzlc5Fs26XrKUYbf1d3Xvi0clwKn8h9bp4Q\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SNao6N1Etzlc5Fs26XrKUYbf1d3Xvi0clwKn8h9bp4Q\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SNao6N1Etzlc5Fs26XrKUYbf1d3Xvi0clwKn8h9bp4Q\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SNao6N1Etzlc5Fs26XrKUYbf1d3Xvi0clwKn8h9bp4Q </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T08:27:57-07:00","id":1302226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301985#post1301985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That aligns with my own experiences. Of particular note, I'm in is Sidereals game and due to that splat's relationship with armour its pretty easy for a single area attack to put most of the circle into negative initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight derail but silken armor is really useful for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T10:43:03-07:00","id":1302265,"title":"","content":"One of our group had it. Unfortunately its expensive and doesn't actually defend against this all that well without some Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T11:45:21-07:00","id":1302286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302265#post1302265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of our group had it. Unfortunately its expensive and doesn't actually defend against this all that well without some Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is the problem with homebrew that's not strong enough for the game atm. Most of which is just a direct port which just can't work in this. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, i feel like the command buff wouldn't be so bad without the other charm that starts with raiton. It's that charm that is a problem because it's just an auto crash waiting to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T11:51:57-07:00","id":1302287,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m also not sure if measuring against what a mid-high Essence Solar can defend is the best yardstick. If your group of DB players comes up against something like that they could well be all dead. I\u2019ll have to think about it more, it\u2019s expensive and not super easy to set up, but it can easily make an attack that only a focused solar has a prayer at defending against, and with enough damage to annihilate anything in a huge radius fairly quickly, before they can run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T12:31:57-07:00","id":1302299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302265#post1302265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of our group had it. Unfortunately its expensive and doesn't actually defend against this all that well without some Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>A much less experienced group of DBs, meanwhile, played by basically the same group, totally wiped out battle groups without any real issue. They cam be really swingy due to their aoe attacks and being able to ignore that generally unreliable nature with a bucket load of auto successes is pretty scary.<br /> <br /> I don't really know how often you can be expected to max out Might, however. I think assuming that that will always be capped may not be accurate, but a single success this way or that also won't change a lot of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T12:32:46-07:00","id":1302300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302286#post1302286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this is the problem with homebrew that's not strong enough for the game atm. Most of which is just a direct port which just can't work in this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm no. Silken Armour is four dot artifact that only gives +5 soak, while there's invariably gaps in out homebrew, the core problem is its expensive and doesn't offer much soak ...unless you homebrew evocations to make it better for this role.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302287#post1302287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m also not sure if measuring against what a mid-high Essence Solar can defend is the best yardstick. If your group of DB players comes up against something like that they could well be all dead. I\u2019ll have to think about it more, it\u2019s expensive and not super easy to set up, but it can easily make an attack that only a focused solar has a prayer at defending against, and with enough damage to annihilate anything in a huge radius fairly quickly, before they can run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, while I'm sure the playtesters tried Lunar elder boss fights I can see them overlooking the potency of an elder Lunar who fights entirely through their bodyguards because its so antithetical to the stereotypical rip and tear that its potentially waiting for someone to mix things up a little then wonder why all their PCs are dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-03-2019, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T12:43:24-07:00","id":1302302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302300#post1302300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm no. Silken Armour is four dot artifact that only gives +4 soak, while there's invariably gaps in out homebrew, the core problem is its expensive and doesn't offer much soak ...unless you homebrew evocations to make it better for this role.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it's 5 soak and 4 hardness that doesn't count as armor. Which is pretty decent could be a little better but the real issue is the homebrew. I've seen a few and they are definitely a good tries but they are direct ports which cannot work in this edition. Not when you are expected to have 20-40 charms (a lot of them which interlock now) in each ability. The holes of the homebrew are extremely large compared to the artifact armor. Silken armor is just one dot higher than normal artifact armor. That's not too expensive. They are also assumed to have evocations. The problem is there's no real example of them. Still sidereals are fun to play so I don't blame you for using homebrew. I just think it's unfair to blame the silken armor.<br /> <br /> Also, again I feel like Raiton\u2019s Banquet Assault is the actual issue. It converts both the attack AND the damage. The ability to turn 16 dice to automatic successes is only a bigger issue because you can combine it with this charm and get 16 automatic successes to the attack and the damage in addition to anything else. While it only works once per scene you can easily use this combo to reset it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-03-2019, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T13:19:30-07:00","id":1302312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301908#post1301908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Command rolls boost attack, not damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point of RBA is that now they boost both. And with IBWE they are successes thus unsoakable.<br /> <br /> Under relatively modest assumptions for an E4 Lunar Warlord, you get about 16 autosuccesses on attack AND damage rolls, and the battle group can roll against every single character it's in contact with. That's before you even roll a die. There is no &quot;well but&quot;; those numbers are wrong, and happily Vance has indicated that they will be fixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","user":"AtG","date":". 04-03-2019, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T13:21:20-07:00","id":1302314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302302#post1302302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean it's 5 soak and 4 hardness that doesn't count as armor. Which is pretty decent could be a little better but the real issue is the homebrew. I've seen a few and they are definitely a good tries but they are direct ports which cannot work in this edition. Not when you are expected to have 20-40 charms (a lot of them which interlock now) in each ability. The holes of the homebrew are extremely large compared to the artifact armor. Silken armor is just one dot higher than normal artifact armor. That's not too expensive. They are also assumed to have evocations. The problem is there's no real example of them. Still sidereals are fun to play so I don't blame you for using homebrew. I just think it's unfair to blame the silken armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incredibly White Room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T13:47:24-07:00","id":1302321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302314#post1302314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is incredibly White Room.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can give my feelings on the homebrew in another thread if you like but this isn't really the place for it any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T13:48:24-07:00","id":1302322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301908#post1301908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Command rolls boost attack, not damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I actually looked at the charms. It does when you use raiton banquet assault. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T14:00:08-07:00","id":1302329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302321#post1302321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can give my feelings on the homebrew in another thread if you like but this isn't really the place for it any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean your thoughts are very white room and 2E.<br /> <br /> The existence of 20-40 Resistance charms does not mean it's trivial for PCs to have them. At 8XP for favored, 20 resistance charms is 160XP. That's enough experience to hit Essence 3 purely in Reistance Charms (chargen charms change this math a bit). This isn't even getting into the idea that some concepts might not have space for Resistance for various reasons (Martial Artists and Crafters can both fall into this due to the cost of EXP sinks), but rather a pure observation on the amount of exp gained.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter how many charms exist in a theoretical tree because most people aren't going to buy charms purely out of one single tree, and that incredible level of depth would make the character incredibly difficult to interact with: as deep as a gorge but as wide as a thimble means sitting out for a majority of time then getting to flex your massive investment once or twice.<br /> <br /> And again, just pure EXP mechanics. 10 Resistance Charms is 80 XP. 20 is 160. If no one is buying 10 resistance charms- ie, if no one is putting over half the budget of reaching Essence 3 in a single charm tree- it doesn't matter if the tree has 10, 15, or 40 charms in it, because most of them probably aren't being used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T14:09:06-07:00","id":1302332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302329#post1302329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I mean your thoughts are very white room and 2E.<br /> <br /> The existence of 20-40 Resistance charms does not mean it's trivial for PCs to have them. At 8XP for favored, 20 resistance charms is 160XP. That's enough experience to hit Essence 3 purely in Reistance Charms (chargen charms change this math a bit). This isn't even getting into the idea that some concepts might not have space for Resistance for various reasons (Martial Artists and Crafters can both fall into this due to the cost of EXP sinks), but rather a pure observation on the amount of exp gained.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter how many charms exist in a theoretical tree because most people aren't going to buy charms purely out of one single tree, and that incredible level of depth would make the character incredibly difficult to interact with: as deep as a gorge but as wide as a thimble means sitting out for a majority of time then getting to flex your massive investment once or twice.<br /> <br /> And again, just pure EXP mechanics. 10 Resistance Charms is 80 XP. 20 is 160. If no one is buying 10 resistance charms- ie, if no one is putting over half the budget of reaching Essence 3 in a single charm tree- it doesn't matter if the tree has 10, 15, or 40 charms in it, because most of them probably aren't being used.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue isn't just the amount of charms but rather the abilities they provide and I haven't seen any sidereal homebrew that's given powers that actually make sidereals around the level of lunars. Moreover, the fatal flaw sidereal homebrew has had is that it's fallen into the same holes that 2e did. A direct port doesn't work from edition to edition. They more than anyone else need to be carefully crafted around the setting. I feel like this isn't the appropriate place to talk about this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-03-2019, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T14:13:59-07:00","id":1302333,"title":"","content":"The real killer here really is the conversion of damage dice to successes, since that makes them post-soak and makes most abilities that are supposed to stop damage unable to interact with them. If it was just bonus attack dice that were converted it would still be incredibly powerfull (like still better than any command boosters solars have) and crash and then kill anyone without a ton of soak from all the extra successes, but not absurdly broken and at least the 30 soak Dawn/Full Moon with Resistance/Stamina charms could survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-03-2019, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T14:27:21-07:00","id":1302337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302333#post1302333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real killer here is the conversion of damage dice to successes, since that makes them post-soak and makes most abilities that are supposed to stop damage unable to interact with them. If it was just bonus attack dice it would still be incredibly powerfull (like still better than any command boosters solars have) and crash and then kill anyone without a ton of soak from all the extra successes, but not absurdly broken and at least the 30 soak Dawn/Full Moon with Resistance/Stamina charms could survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does ruin abasing shrug interact with that? does it make the lunar reroll those successes or does no longer apply. Outside of resistance or SSE. Dodge had 3m for -1 successes but that's expensive and I don't know how it would stop this many successes from crashing them. I don't think has melee something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T14:27:21-07:00","id":1302338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302332#post1302332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue isn't just the amount of charms but rather the abilities they provide and I haven't seen any sidereal homebrew that's given powers that actually make sidereals around the level of lunars. Moreover, the fatal flaw sidereal homebrew has had is that it's fallen into the same holes that 2e did. A direct port doesn't work from edition to edition. They more than anyone else need to be carefully crafted around the setting. I feel like this isn't the appropriate place to talk about this</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about theoretical gaps based on bringing over charms directly. I'm talking about specifically the investment of exp in an actual, played character and how much they get and where they spend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T14:36:18-07:00","id":1302340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302338#post1302338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not talking about theoretical gaps based on bringing over charms directly. I'm talking about specifically the investment of exp in an actual, played character and how much they get and where they spend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about issues that solars and lunars have tools to deal with at low essence that sidereals flat out do not. More than just that I'm also talking about how the low number of charms makes Martial arts the end all be all. With 20-40 charms in every tree you have more options you have things that improve native charms, it also lets you branch into trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T14:45:43-07:00","id":1302343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302337#post1302337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dodge had 3m for -1 successes but that's expensive and I don't know how it would stop this many successes from crashing them</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean Rumor of Form that requires them to roll a ridiculous number of 1s to ever be meaninfull.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302337#post1302337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does ruin abasing shrug interact with that? does it make the lunar reroll those successes or does no longer apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't know, but rerolling sort of implies that dice were rolled in the first place. Even if it does work its only once per scene.<br /> <br /> Damage auto-successes is just not something that charms seem to have been designed to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 04-03-2019, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T14:47:57-07:00","id":1302344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302343#post1302343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you mean Rumor of Form that requires them to roll a ridiculous number of 1s to ever be meaninfull.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't realize that. Yeah the ability to remove the need for dice from the roll is way too good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-03-2019, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T08:18:03-07:00","id":1302558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302340#post1302340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about issues that solars and lunars have tools to deal with at low essence that sidereals flat out do not. More than just that I'm also talking about how the low number of charms makes Martial arts the end all be all. With 20-40 charms in every tree you have more options you have things that improve native charms, it also lets you branch into trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to figure out how to respond to this and basically the best way I can say it is this<br /> <br /> You're assuming a direct copy of 2E charms into 3E without actually seeing the charmset being played with, while failing to understand what I'm talking about is the amount of EXP spent on a character is not an infinite resource, and that this means that players will have different investments in abilities. You're just blanketly assuming that every Sidereal homebrew is the same, but that's not even completely relevant to the discussion I'm having so much as a consistent point of confusion in how I read your post. Lioness never really brought up what her charmset she had access to looked like, so you just defaulted to the worst interpretation of it; that it was a mostly copied version of 2E Sidereals rather then an attempt to fit them into 3E. The truth is that what it is doesn't matter, but if you go into the discussion with that as the assumption of what's being argued instead of a discussion on the expenditure of EXP, you're going to end up missing or deflecting the points someone else is trying to make because you're discussing something that isn't directly relevant to the discussion.<br /> <br /> What I'm talking about is the EXP investment in getting new abilities and raising them and buying charms. 9 charms is still 72 EXP, a significant investment. I would argue something like 3-5 Resistance charms is a decent idea of how many charms a combat character who primarily relies on parry or dodge might have around Essence 3, and they might be purchased from Non-Caste/Favored. This would be around 24-40 for Favored, and 30-50 for Non-Favored. I think this may still not really be accurate but it depends on the game; a character's build path never survives interaction with how the ST plays the game unless you're really hardheaded, and your builds will adapt to be more appropriate to how the ST runs the game; in some games, the combat king character may just be the person who has spent 100 EXP, while in others it may be someone whose spent half their EXP on it. This isn't even getting into the fact that, arguably, we aren't really discussing the super heavy combat focus but rather someone who might be on the second level of combat effectiveness; someone who isn't a drag on combat but isn't intending to be the one getting into fistfights with elder lunars and tangling with third circle demons, but rather just someone who has maybe an artifact and some charms, but that's tangential here.<br /> <br /> What does 3-5 Resistance charms get a Solar? Especially, what does it get when the Exalt in question probably doesn't have Resistance 5 or Stamina 5, and is instead maybe sitting around both at 3ish. I'm just gonna use 3 here because honestly it makes my argument better, but thanks to MadLetter's excellent charm cascades you can look at these numbers really easily. Also because, if you look at the charms, once you pass the third charm it's expecting you to have 4s and 5s in your Resistance. In this idea, our hypothetical Solar might not even have Resistance 4.<br /> <br /> A Solar could get to Iron Skin Concentration, giving them maybe 3 extra -0 health levels, the ability to pay 3 motes to increase her soak by 3, and another 3m to increase her soak by 2 . Or they could have purchased maybe 3 Ox-Body techniques, giving them 9 extra Health Levels; 3 -1s and 6 -2s. Those aren't awful. You can do okay and maybe survive a hit from a battle group that rolled poorly when it hit you, maybe. The best hope is that it just doesn't hit you, though, because the inert initiative also means the battlegroup isn't really suffering penalties for 'decisive' attacking you; after all, they just do their damage. The Solar isn't fully immune to battle groups, far from it even, and by that logic, it is unlikely a Sidereal will be immune to it either; they're supposed to be weaker, even if the power tiers have been shortened.<br /> <br /> These aren't going to 100% protect you from the Battle Group, and one thing I've noticed is a cycle effect can sometimes happen; where the Exalt is crashed by the Battle Group, then has to attack the non-battle group opponent to get the Initiative so the Battle Group doesn't rock them.<br /> <br /> This is intended; Battle Groups can be incredibly dangerous if you aren't careful because their AOE attacks and ability to deal damage no matter their Initiative means they can threaten any opponent who happens to be crashed, which can also turn off some of the more powerful defensive charms thanks to the Perilous keyword. They are always going to be more swingy then a normal attacker because they attack more then one person and this innately increases the RNG; no longer is it one person being hit by a fantastic attack roll, but instead an entire group can be hit by one. When this is combined with a massive pool of Automatic successes on Attack rolls and Damage rolls, you remove any of the swingy results that generally result in battlegroups being less effective, but you also turn off a lot of- just in this example- Solar Resistance charms that expect there to be damage dice instead of a bunch of automatic successes. Even a Solar in Aegis of Invincible Might is only protected from 5 levels of the automatic damage, but that's not related to my point.<br /> <br /> My point more is your observation of 'well there's 20 to 40 charms' isn't relevant, and shouldn't be looked at like that. An Exalt isn't going to have all the charms in the Resistance tree, they're going to have some, maybe, if they've gotten to that level of investment and they wanted those charms, so looking at every Resistance charm and assuming any Exalt worth their salt would just have the entire tree is basically going very 2E, where the assumed play pattern was 'I'm going to go into my time manipulating Manse and sit there until I get 500EXP before I start playing.', because the trees were much, much smaller and the game, towards the end of it's life cycle, encouraged that style of play.<br /> <br /> This is important because NPCs can have a pretty large amount of EXP versus a PC, particularly those designed to be bosses for a group of PCs, since they need a lot of attack and defense charms to get over the base effects of being severely outnumbered; though they may have allies, you never want your big boss man to get owned first, after all-, and often times are older; especially for, let's say, a Dragonblooded Wyld Hunt going to attack a Lunar Elder, this charm could turn the already swingy Battlegroups which can sometimes turn a fight into 'oh crud we just all got crashed at once by the battle group' into 'oh shit this battle group is literally killing us by itself'. Stuff like that can really surprise the group as a whole and require some quick runbacks.<br /> <br /> This is a mess of a whole bunch of conflicting and overlapping factors going on here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T08:30:51-07:00","id":1302563,"title":"","content":"My first point, which I will say as bluntly as possible. Is that the homebrew for sidereals isn't good enough for the level that it needs to be. Lionness is having this issue because we do not have a charmset that properly compliments the sidereal powerset in 3e. The ones we have have been good tries but not at the level it needs to. Moreover, she was blaming Silken armor for not being good enough when it's not the problem of the armor it's the problem with what we currently have to work with when it comes to sidereals. To be fair, it takes a lot of work to make a good charmset so I don't blame the people who tried.<br /> <br /> <br /> My second point about battle groups was to get back on topic. Converting all your dice to automatic successes is enough to crash anyone who's not supernal melee even they might not be able to stop it because it basically prevents the defenses which work on 1s and 2s to apply. A lot of the defenses are conditional now and Raiton Banquet assault and the commanding buff charm do too much together. Not only that but they stack. IF you use them together and then crash an opponent, Raiton's banquet assault resets and can be used again. Cascading into more damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-04-2019, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T10:15:46-07:00","id":1302600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1302300#post1302300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, while I'm sure the playtesters tried Lunar elder boss fights I can see them overlooking the potency of an elder Lunar who fights entirely through their bodyguards because its so antithetical to the stereotypical rip and tear that its potentially waiting for someone to mix things up a little then wonder why all their PCs are dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can definitely see that happening. Like maybe the ST is running a late Essence DB game, and they\u2019ve set up the scene so that the five Essence 5 PCs and their army are squaring off against the Lunar and his army and then by turn two all the characters are crashed to oblivion and their army has evaporated. Or the same with an early Essence Solar game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T11:33:13-07:00","id":1302879,"title":"","content":"Forgot to address this. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1301844-a-couple-lunar-charms-that-are-concerning?p=1301905#post1301905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't that kind of create an incentive to fight armies with armies?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not exactly. Bringing a battle group of your own doesn't stop the area attack from hitting everyone in range and is an aspect of their rules that might merit further attention if enormous bonuses for battle groups are the wave of the future.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}